// Task: ZP-TBD-1 follow-up (Andrea, 2026-08-14: "Amber integration is still not
// working... KM should be updated in the police invoice as quantity. This is now
// the 4th time this has been looked at.")
//
// Zoho App: CRM
// Module: none directly (standalone function, invoked by Amber's own callback)
// Function Name: standalone.amberConnectResponse
// Trigger Source: Amber Connect posts here directly after every completed job.
//   POST https://www.zohoapis.com/crm/v7/functions/amberconnectresponse/actions/execute
//        ?auth_type=apikey&zapikey=<inline key, masked>
//   This is documented in "AmberConnect - Zoho_Amber Integration Document_v1.0",
//   section 9 (page 20-22), provided by Andrea 2026-08-14.
//
// WHY THIS WAS MISSED THREE TIMES BEFORE:
// ZP-TBD-1 (2026-07-03, this same repo folder) investigated createJobInAmber and
// sendCompleteStatusToAmber -- both are the ZOHO -> AMBER direction (creating jobs,
// telling Amber a trip started/finished). Its metadata.md even concludes:
//   "Number_of_distance_in_km does not come back from Amber on Police cases...
//    the completion payload has no distance/mileage field at all."
// That conclusion was correct for the functions it looked at, but WRONG about Amber
// overall -- Amber sends KM back through a DIFFERENT, separate callback
// (amberConnectResponse) that nobody had traced until this pass. All three prior
// "fixes" very likely re-touched sendCompleteStatusToAmber / createJobInAmber, which
// were never where the KM problem lived.
//
// ================= THE ACTUAL BUG =================
// Amber's payload (section 9 of their doc) is a JSON array of ~34 named fields, with
// "TotalDistanceKM" as the LAST key. The live amberConnectResponse function does not
// parse JSON by field name at all -- it splits the raw request body into segments on
// multipart boundary markers and grabs distanceKm by COUNTING FROM THE END:
//     distanceKm = valueData.get(valueData.size() - 2);   // "second from last"
// Per Amber's current payload, "second from last" is LastUpdatedDateTime, not
// TotalDistanceKM (which is now the very last field). So the function has been
// writing a DATE STRING into the KM field's source variable, which likely produces
// either an error swallowed by the outer try/catch (see empty catch block) or a
// nonsense value -- either way, Trips.Number_of_distance_in_km never gets Amber's
// real KM. This is a pure ordering bug: if Amber ever changes their field order
// again, whatever field happens to be second-from-last breaks it again, silently.
//
// ================= THE FIX =================
// Read TotalDistanceKM by searching for its literal field name in the raw request
// body, not by counting positions. This is immune to Amber reordering fields, adding
// new ones, or removing ones DFH doesn't use.
//
// Everything else in the function (the job-token extraction used to find the Trip,
// the Trip_Status update, the workflow trigger) is UNCHANGED -- only the KM line is
// touched, because that is the only piece confirmed broken.
//
// TO DEPLOY: paste this whole function over the live standalone.amberConnectResponse.
// TO TEST: trigger a real (or Amber-sandbox) Police job completion with a nonzero
// TotalDistanceKM, and confirm Trips.Number_of_distance_in_km updates to that value
// (see test-cases.md in this folder).

string standalone.amberConnectResponse(String crmAPIRequest)
{
	apiRequest = crmAPIRequest.toMap();
	bodyText = apiRequest.get("body");

	// ---- existing job-token extraction (Trip match) -- UNCHANGED, still working ----
	parts = bodyText.toList("Content-Disposition: attachment; name=\"0\"");
	valueData = List();
	for each  part in parts
	{
		trimmed = part.trim();
		if(trimmed.contains("--------------------------"))
		{
			trimmed = trimmed.toList("--------------------------").get(0).trim();
		}
		valueData.add(trimmed);
	}
	tempData = List();
	foundFirst = false;
	for each  value in valueData
	{
		if(value != "")
		{
			foundFirst = true;
		}
		if(foundFirst)
		{
			tempData.add(value);
		}
	}
	valueData = tempData;

	try
	{
		jobToken = valueData.get(0);
		// Reference ID

		// ---- FIX (2026-08-14): read TotalDistanceKM by its literal field name
		// in the raw body instead of the old "second-from-last split segment"
		// guess. See the header comment above for why the old logic broke.
		distanceKm = 0;
		if(bodyText.contains("TotalDistanceKM"))
		{
			afterKey = bodyText.toList("TotalDistanceKM").get(1);
			// afterKey now starts right after the key, e.g. ' : 2.3\r\n\t}\r\n]'
			afterKey = afterKey.toList(":").get(1);
			numStr = "";
			chars = afterKey.toList("");
			for each  ch in chars
			{
				if((ch >= "0" && ch <= "9") || ch == ".")
				{
					numStr = numStr + ch;
				}
				else if(numStr != "")
				{
					break;
				}
			}
			if(numStr != "")
			{
				distanceKm = numStr.toDecimal();
			}
		}

		searchTrip = zoho.crm.searchRecords("Trips","(Amber_Connect_Job_ID:equals:" + jobToken + ")",1,1);
		if(searchTrip.size() > 0)
		{
			tripMap = Map();
			tripMap.put("Trip_Status","Completed");
			tripMap.put("Number_of_distance_in_km",distanceKm);
			info tripMap;
			result = zoho.crm.updateRecord("Trips",searchTrip.get(0).get("id"),tripMap,{"trigger":{"workflow"}});
			info result;
		}
		else
		{
			info "No trip found for Job Token: " + jobToken;
		}
	}
	catch (e)
	{
		info e;
	}
	return "";
}
